  "text":"7.1.1 How to Use the Plug/Jack List and Locations To find which position to install specific connectors to, refer to the table \"7.1.x.1 Plug/Jack Location List\" for Figure No. and Item No., and then to the figure in \"7.1.x.2 Plug/Jack Locations\".P/J No. on \"7.1.x.1 Plug/Jack Location List\" is expressed in the nine ways below:P/J250 represents Plug/Jack 250.P250 represents Plug 250.J250 represents Jack 250.DP250 represents Double Plug 250.DJ250 represents Double Jack 250.CN1 represents Connector 1.FS1 represents Faston Terminal 1.SJ1 represents Shorting Jack 1.T1 represents Terminal 1.(Figure 1) 710001"
