  "text":"REP 27.29.4 (SCC) Inlet Reference PL:PL 27.29Removal Perform the Power OFF procedure at the IOT. Check that the power is OFF and unplug the Power Plug.Static electricity may damage electrical parts. Static electricity may damage electrical parts. Always wear a wrist band during servicing. If a wrist band is not available, touch some metallic parts before servicing to discharge the static electricity.Remove the Top Cover Assembly. (PL 27.15)Remove the Rear Upper Cover Assembly. (PL 27.16)Remove the Rear Lower Cover. (PL 27.16)Remove the (SCC) Inlet Bracket. (Figure 1)Disconnect the connector (x2) behind the (SCC) Inlet. (Harness in which black is top, and white is bottom)Disconnect the Earth Connector.Disconnect the connector at the right side of the (SCC) Inlet.Remove the screw (x2).Remove the (SCC) Inlet Bracket.(Figure 1) ff427154Remove the (SCC) Inlet from the Bracket. (Figure 2)Remove the hook (x3).Remove the (SCC) Inlet.(Figure 2) ff427155InstallationCheck the marking behind the Inlet, and install correctly. (Figure 3)L: Black wire (Top)N: White wire (Bottom)(Figure 3) ff427181"
