  "text":"REP 39.39.1 Left Stacker Belt Reference PL:PL 39.39Removal After turning OFF the Power Switch, check that the screen display goes off and the [Power Saver] button stops blinking. Then, turn OFF the Main Power Switch, check that the [Main Power] lamp has turned OFF, and then turn OFF the Breaker and unplug the Power Plug.Detach the HCS from upstream device. (REP 39.1.1)Remove the Rear Cover. (REP 39.2.2)Remove the Upper Cover. (REP 39.4.1)Remove the Tamper Unit. (REP 39.28.1)Remove the Paddle. (REP 39.24.2)Remove the Stacker Exit Roll Housing. (REP 39.25.1)Remove the Edge Sensor Frame. (REP 39.25.2)Remove the Stacker Left Lower Cover. (Figure 1)Remove the Front Door Stopper Screw.Remove the screw (x4).Remove the Stacker Left Lower Cover.(Figure 1) sa49918Remove the screw that secure the Stack No Paper Sensor. (Figure 2)Remove the screw (x2).Move the Stack No Paper Sensor.(Figure 2) sa49952Remove the Stack No Paper Sensor. (Figure 3)Disconnect the connector (J329L).Disconnect the connector (J329P).(Figure 3) sa49953Remove the Stacker Left Center Cover. (Figure 4)Remove the screw (x4).Remove the Stacker Left Center Cover.(Figure 4) sa43998Remove the Stacker Left Lower Frame. (Figure 5)Remove the screw (M4: x5).Remove the Stacker Left Lower Frame.(Figure 5) sa49919Remove the Front Rail Support. (Figure 6)Remove the screw (M3: x7).Remove the screw (M4: x7).Remove the Front Rail Support.(Figure 6) sa49920Remove the Rear Rail Support. (Figure 7)Remove the screw (M3: x7).Remove the screw (M4: x6).Remove the Rear Rail Support.(Figure 7) sa49921Remove the Left Tray Arm. (Figure 8)Remove the screw (x4).Remove the Belt Clamp (x2).Remove the Left Tray Arm.(Figure 8) sa49922Remove the Pulley Bracket. (Figure 9)Remove the screw (M4: x8).Remove the Pulley Bracket (x2).(Figure 9) sa49923Remove the Left Stacker Belt. (Figure 10)Remove the clip (x8).Remove the gear and the key.Remove the Bearing (x2).Move Shaft in the direction of the arrow to remove the Left Stacker Belt (x2).(Figure 10) sa49924InstallationWhen installing the Left Tray Arm, perform the Left/Right Tray Arm Installation Position. (ADJ 39.39.1)"
