  "text":"REP 39.40.1 Right Stacker Belt Reference PL:PL 39.40Removal After turning OFF the Power Switch, check that the screen display goes off and the [Power Saver] button stops blinking. Then, turn OFF the Main Power Switch, check that the [Main Power] lamp has turned OFF, and then turn OFF the Breaker and unplug the Power Plug.Detach the HCS from upstream device. (REP 39.1.1)Remove the Rear Cover. (REP 39.2.2)Remove the Upper Cover. (REP 39.4.1)Remove the Tamper Unit. (REP 39.28.1)Remove the Stacker Right Front Cover. (Figure 1)Remove the screw (x5).Remove the Stacker Right Front Cover.(Figure 1) sa49925Remove the Front Door Lock Bracket. (Figure 2)Remove the screw (x4).Remove the Front Door Lock Bracket.(Figure 2) sa49926Disconnect the Front Door Lock Bracket connector. (Figure 3)Disconnect the connector (x2).Release the clamp (x3) and remove the wire harness.(Figure 3) sa49927Remove the Stacker Right Lower Cover. (Figure 4)Remove the screw (x4).Remove the Stacker Right Lower Cover.(Figure 4) sa49928Remove the Stacker Right Center Cover. (Figure 5)Remove the screw (x4).Remove the Stacker Right Center Cover.(Figure 5) sa43999Remove the Stacker Right Rear Cover. (Figure 6)Remove the screw (x5).Remove the Stacker Right Rear Cover.(Figure 6) sa49929Remove the Stacker Right Lower Frame. (Figure 7)Remove the screw (M4: x4).Remove the Stacker Right Lower Frame.(Figure 7) sa49930Remove the Front Rail Support. (Figure 8)Remove screw (M3: x7).Remove screw (M4: x7).Remove the Front Rail Support.(Figure 8) sa49932Remove the Rear Rail Support. (Figure 9)Remove the screw (M3: x7).Remove the screw (M4: x6).Remove the Rear Rail Support.(Figure 9) sa49933Remove the Right Tray Arm. (Figure 10)Remove the screw (x4).Remove the Belt Clamp (x2).Remove the Right Tray Arm.(Figure 10) sa49934Remove the Pulley Bracket. (Figure 11)Remove the screw (M4: x8).Remove the Pulley Bracket (x2).(Figure 11) sa49935At the rear of the HCS, remove the screws that secure the Roll Cover. (Figure 12)Remove the Tapping Screw (x2).(Figure 12) sa49936Remove the Roll Cover. (Figure 13)Remove the Tapping Screw (x2).Remove the Roll Cover.(Figure 13) sa49937Remove the Right Stacker Belt. (Figure 14)Remove the clip (x8).Remove the gear and the key.Remove the Bearing (x2).Move Shaft in the direction of the arrow to remove the Right Stacker Belt (x2).(Figure 14) sa49938InstallationWhen installing the Right Tray Arm, perform the installation position for Left/Right Tray Arm. (ADJ 39.39.1)"
