  "text":"ADJ 76.3.1 Rewriting NVM Value When Replacing 1ST Lamp Assembly PurposeWhen replacing the 1ST Lamp Assembly, rewrite the NVM value.ProcedureCheck the LED Color Rank Value indicated on the LED PWB of the 1ST Lamp Assembly to be installed.(Figure 1) ism476501Enter DC131 NVM Read/Write and rewrite the value of NVM [580-001] to the value listed in the following table according to the LED Color Rank Value indicated on the LED PWB.NVM valueLED Color Rank ValueNVM valueLED Color Rank Value000(Not applicable)010(Not applicable)001J1D/J11D011K1D/K11D002J1E/J11E012K1E/K11E003J1F/J11F013K1F/K11F004J1G/J11G014K1G/K11G005J1H/J11H015K1H/K11H006J1J (Not selected)016K1J (Not selected)007J1K/J11K017K1K/K11K008J1L (Not selected)018K1L (Not selected)009J1M/J11M019K1M/K11MIn the example in Figure 1, the LED Color Rank Value is [K11H], so the value of NVM is rewritten to [015].Turn the power OFF and ON."
